  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether the linear PCA encoder is a bottleneck for the RNA signal. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates the effect of switching from a linear PCA encoder to a learned non-linear scvi representation while keeping profile setting identical to config_001. If scvi improves accuracy, it informs encoder choice for all downstream multimodal experiments; if not, PCA is sufficient and we can focus budget on profile/aggregation/fusion choices. This is the highest-information single-variable test available and the best use of experiment 3 with 7 remaining."
}

